      <section class="ent-sec ent-sec--first ent-sec--trust" id="security" aria-labelledby="sec-h">
        <h1 class="ent-eyebrow" id="sec-h">Security and privacy</h1>
        <h3 class="ent-h">Your data stays yours, on a private server in your own cloud.</h3>
        <p class="ent-body">OpenShore works inside the systems that hold your pay, revenue and customer records, so it starts at the strictest setting and only you can open it up.</p>
{% include "ill-security.njk" %}
        <ul class="ent-secgrid" role="list">
          <li>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 18h10.5a4 4 0 0 0 .4-8A6 6 0 0 0 6.3 9.2 4.4 4.4 0 0 0 7 18z" /></svg>
            <h4>Runs in your own cloud</h4>
            <p>Every company gets its own OpenShore server, in its own cloud account. Your chats, files and records stay there, not in ours.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8" cy="15" r="4" /><path d="M11 12l8.5-8.5M16 7l2.5 2.5M13.5 9.5l2 2" /></svg>
            <h4>Your models, your keys</h4>
            <p>Bots run on the model providers you choose, with keys kept in your own secret store. Switch providers whenever you like.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" /><path d="M7.8 12.3l2.8 2.8 5.6-5.8" /></svg>
            <h4>A person approves every change</h4>
            <p>Bots propose and people decide. Anything that changes pay needs your revenue owner’s sign-off first.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="3.5" width="14" height="17" rx="2.5" /><path d="M8.5 8.5h7m-7 3.5h7m-7 3.5h4" /></svg>
            <h4>Every action on the record</h4>
            <p>An append-only audit log records what ran, which model it used, who approved it and what changed, including anything our team does.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="10.5" width="14" height="10" rx="2.5" /><path d="M8.5 10.5V8a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 7 0v2.5" /></svg>
            <h4>Your sign-in, your permissions</h4>
            <p>People sign in through your identity provider, like Google Workspace, Microsoft Entra ID or Okta, and the server enforces who sees what. No one sees another person’s pay or quota.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="ent-body"><b>Privacy first.</b> Your data stays in your cloud, on your keys, and goes only to the AI models you choose. We never sell it or use it to train AI models.</p>
        <p class="ent-body"><b>Access only to serve you.</b> By default we see service telemetry, like errors, uptime and versions, with no customer content. When we need to look at your data to set up, fix or improve a bot, it’s with your permission, limited to that task, and logged. You can turn our access off at any time.</p>
        <p class="ent-note ent-sec-ask">Design partners get the full architecture and security review before anything is installed. <a href="mailto:{{ site.enterpriseContact }}?subject={{ 'Security review: OpenShore' | urlencode }}">Ask for it <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></p>
      </section>
